event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":86,"item_id":"rs_06a5cb0758df242f016ac940b580bc8196a9c4ec74a3602787","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering testing strategies**\n\nI'm thinking about how we can add browser script simulated tests in a virtual machine with a small Element implementation. It would help us verify UI regression while keeping everything in memory. The specification indicates that automation is useful, yet it seems we don't currently have tests. That's interesting because maybe we could add unit tests to the client VM, keeping it around 100 lines to make it manageable. It feels like a good approach!"}

